A: Absolutely. The system provides multiple organization methods:
Frameworks - Top-level containers for KPI collections. For example, you might have a "Commercial Framework v1.0" and a "Startup Growth Framework v2.0." Frameworks have versioning, so you can evolve your KPIs over time while maintaining historical versions.
Sectors - High-level categorization by organization type: Commercial, NGO, Public Sector, and Consulting. Each sector has tailored KPI templates and recommended threshold configurations.
Categories - Hierarchical groupings within frameworks. For example:
•	Financial Performance (Revenue, Margins, Cost Control)
•	Impact & Outcomes (Beneficiaries, Program Completion)
•	Operational Efficiency (Process Times, Quality Metrics)
•	Customer & Stakeholder (Satisfaction, Retention)
