Part 2: Targets & Phasing
Q6: How do we set targets? Can we set monthly targets?
A: Setting targets is flexible and powerful.
Annual Targets - First, you set annual targets for each KPI and user. For example, "John should achieve 15 million KES in revenue for 2025."
Monthly Phasing - Then, you distribute that annual target across the 12 months. This is critical for organizations with seasonal patterns. For example, a retail business might allocate only 5% of the annual revenue target to January, but 14% to December.
The system provides three phasing strategies:
Equal Split - Distributes the annual target equally across all 12 months. Simple and predictable.
Seasonal Distribution - Uses predefined weights based on historical patterns. You can customize the weights for each month.
Custom Pattern - You manually define the target for each month. The system shows you the distribution visually and ensures the sum matches your annual target.
Once a performance cycle begins, phasing is locked and cannot be changed. This ensures data integrity - you can't change targets after the fact to make performance look better.
You can also batch update targets via CSV import, making bulk target setting efficient for large organizations.
Q7: What is target cascading and how does it work?
A: Target cascading is the process of breaking down organization-level targets to departments, teams, and finally individuals.
Here's how it works:
1.	Organization Target: The executive team sets a company-wide target (e.g., "Company revenue: 100 million KES")
2.	Cascade to Departments: The system distributes the 100 million across departments. You can use different distribution rules:
o	Equal split (each department gets the same)
o	Weighted by headcount (larger departments get larger targets)
o	Weighted by budget (departments with bigger budgets get bigger targets)
o	Custom percentages (you define exactly how much each department contributes)
3.	Cascade to Teams: Within each department, the department target is further broken down to teams.
4.	Cascade to Individuals: Finally, team targets are distributed to individual team members.
The system tracks the entire cascade tree visually. You can see at a glance how organization targets flow down to each person.
If a target changes at a higher level, the system can automatically recascade to lower levels, maintaining consistency throughout the organization.
The cascade history is fully audited, so you can see who initiated the cascade, when it happened, and what the resulting targets were.
Q8: What happens if we miss a target? Can we adjust targets mid-year?
A: The system handles target adjustments with proper controls.
Pending Adjustments - If you need to adjust a target mid-year, you submit an adjustment request. This requires approval from the dashboard champion or appropriate manager. The request must include a reason for the adjustment.
Approval Workflow - The approver reviews the request and can approve, reject, or request modifications. Approved adjustments are applied to the target, and the system recalculates scores automatically.
Audit Trail - All adjustments are fully audited. You can see the original target, the adjusted target, who requested it, who approved it, when it happened, and why.
Locked Periods - For past periods that have been closed (typically after 3 months), adjustments are not allowed. This ensures data integrity for reporting.
Exception Handling - In cases of data entry errors, you can request an adjustment to actual data rather than changing the target. This is the preferred approach because it maintains target integrity while correcting mistakes.
The system also provides trend analysis that highlights when targets are consistently being missed, helping you identify whether the targets are unrealistic or whether performance needs improvement.
