Q18: How do aggregated scores work for teams and departments?
A: The system automatically rolls up scores at every level.
Individual Level - Each person has a weighted average score based on their KPIs and assigned weights.
Team Level - Team score is the average of all team members' scores. You can see which team members are above or below team average.
Department Level - Department score is the weighted average of teams within the department (weighted by team size).
Organization Level - Organization health score is the weighted average of departments (weighted by department size).
Example Rollup:
•	Department A (50 employees): Score 85%
•	Department B (30 employees): Score 92%
•	Department C (20 employees): Score 78%
•	Organization Health: (85×50 + 92×30 + 78×20) ÷ 100 = 85.1%
Drill-Down - From any aggregated score, you can click through to see the underlying components:
•	Organization → Departments → Teams → Individuals → KPIs → Monthly data
This hierarchical viewing works from any level. A CEO can see organization health, click to a department, click to a team within that department, click to an employee, and see their individual KPI details.
All aggregations update in real-time as data is entered and approved.
