Part 11: Data Quality & Integrity
Q34: How does the system prevent data entry errors?
A: Multiple safeguards protect data quality.
Input Validation:
•	Data type checking (ensures numbers are numbers)
•	Range validation (warns if value is unusually high/low)
•	Required field enforcement
•	Format validation for percentages, currencies, etc.
Business Rule Validation:
•	Percentage KPIs cannot exceed 100%
•	Financial KPIs cannot be negative (unless allowed)
•	Milestone KPIs accept only 0 or 100
•	Time KPIs accept only positive numbers
Duplicate Prevention:
•	Cannot submit twice for same KPI and period
•	Bulk uploads detect and prevent duplicates
•	Warning before overwriting existing data
Evidence Requirements:
•	Configurable evidence requirements per KPI
•	Managers can require documentation for certain metrics
•	Missing evidence triggers warning or blocks submission
Supervisor Validation:
•	All data requires supervisor approval before going live
•	Rejected entries require correction and resubmission
•	Approval is not automatic (except for trusted auto-approval rules)
Audit Trail:
•	Every change is logged with timestamp and user
•	Original values are preserved before updates
•	Full history available for review
These safeguards ensure that only accurate, validated data appears in dashboards and reports.
Q35: What happens if incorrect data is approved?
A: The system provides correction workflows.
Adjustment Request:
•	Employee or manager can request adjustment to approved data
•	Request requires reason for change
•	Dashboard champion or senior manager must approve
Adjustment Record:
•	Original value is preserved in history
•	Adjusted value becomes the active data
•	Both values are visible in audit trail
•	Reason for adjustment is documented
Score Recalculation:
•	When adjusted data is approved, scores automatically recalculate
•	Traffic lights update immediately
•	Aggregations refresh
•	Historical trends are updated
Notification:
•	Relevant stakeholders receive notification of adjustment
•	Dashboard champion is informed of any approved changes
•	Audit log shows who approved the adjustment and why
Time Limits:
•	Adjustments typically allowed within 90 days
•	Older data may be locked (configurable)
•	Permanent locks after audit period (e.g., after fiscal year close)
This ensures data can be corrected when mistakes happen while maintaining audit integrity.
